                    %a{:href => "#D6D8BoundStatesWithDefects"} D6-D8-brane bound states with D2-D4-brane defects
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#d4d8brane_bound_states_with_d2d6brane_defects"} D4-D8-brane bound states with D2-D6-brane defects
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#kkmonopole"} KK-Monopole
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#mtheorystrong_coupling_limit"} M-Theory/Strong coupling limit
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesLiftToMTheory"} Lift to M-theory
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em massive type IIA string theory
            is a deformation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            which contains the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+forms"} flux forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0
            and/or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duality"} Hodge dually
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 10
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{10}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"} massive type IIA supergravity
            in analogy to how plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            of plain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+supergravity"} type IIA supergravity
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#black_d8branes Black D8-branes
          %p
            It is (only) massive type IIA string theory where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            exist as actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#BergshoessdeRooGreenPapadopoulosTownsend96"}> BdRGPT96 96
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ChamblinPerry97"} Chamblin-Perry 97
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#JanssenMeessenOrtin99"} Janssen-Meessen-Ortin 99
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8-brane+bound+states"} D6-D8-brane bound states
            (
            %a{:href => "#Singh02a"}> Singh 02a
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Singh02b"} Singh 02b
          %p
            This is because the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            around a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
            (with its 9-dimensional
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D8-brane charge
            is measured by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            0-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+form"} flux form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duality"} Hodge dual
            10-form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 10
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{10}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            in the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D10+supergravity"} D=10 supergravity
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romans+supergravity"}> Romans supergravity
            ”) and causes the mass term for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
          %h3#lift_to_mtheory Lift to M-theory?
          %p
            The massive version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+type+IIA+string+theory+and+M-theory"} duality between type IIA string theory and M-theory
            is more subtle, since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            does not admit a corresponding mass deformation (
            %a{:href => "#BDHS97"}> BDHS 97
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Deser97"} Deser 97
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Tsimpis05"} Tsimpis 05
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#AJTZ10"} AJTZ10
            it was argued that a massive strong-coupling limit may just not exist.
          %p
            But in
            %a{:href => "#Hull98"} Hull 98
            an embedding of massive IIA into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            was claimed, and a corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            compactification was claimed in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LoweNastaeRamgoolam03"} Lowe-Nastae-Ramgoolam 03
          %p
            More concretely,
            %a{:href => "#HenneauxJamsinKleinschmidtPersson09"} Henneaux, Jamsin, Kleinschmidt &amp; Persson 2009
            find a sector of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"} massive type IIA supergravity
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E10"} E10
            = succeed "-covariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"} massive type IIA supergravity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"}> D8-brane
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%28-2%29-brane"} D(-2)-brane
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p An early hint is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
              , p. 8,9 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dirichlet-Branes and Ramond-Ramond Charges
              %strong 7
              5 (1995) 4724-4727 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510017"}> arXiv:hep-th/9510017
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Serious development in
          %ul
            %li#BergshoeffdeBooGreenPapadopoulosTownsend96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
              , Mees de Roo,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"} Michael Green
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Papadopoulos"} George Papadopoulos
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality of Type II 7-branes and 8-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9601150"} arXiv:hep-th/9601150
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Michael Haack,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Louis"} Jan Louis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harvendra+Singh"} Harvendra Singh
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Massive Type IIA Theory on K3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0102110"} arXiv:hep-th/0102110
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harvendra+Singh"}> Harvendra Singh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Romans type IIA theory and the heterotic strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201206"} arXiv:hep-th/0201206
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
                , K. van den Broek,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Massive IIA flux compactifications and U-dualities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0611185"} arXiv:hep-th/0611185
          %h3#black_branes Black branes
          %h4#d8branes D8-branes
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
            was identified as a solution to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romans+supergravity"} Romans supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+string+theory"} massive type IIA string theory
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#BergshoeffdeBooGreenPapadopoulosTownsend96"} Bergshoeff-de Boo-Green-Papadopoulos-Townsend 96
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#ChamblinPerry97
              %p
                A. Chamblin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malcolm+Perry"} Malcolm Perry
                %em Dynamic D8-branes in IIA string theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9712112"}> arXiv:hep-th/9712112
                )
